hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-19 = unlines (cons "Kinship goes deeper than humanity, which brings us to Gaia. *Human* is from *humus*, earth. The Hebrew story says it in its own language: *adam*, the first human, is named from *adamah*, the ground. Two independent traditions named the human being an earthling. The Gaian superorganism is in the name of the species in at least two languages. The thesis that human knowledge begins with Gaian knowledge is, in the words, a tautology the ancients already wrote down: the earth-born know what the earth taught." nil)
